.\" Man page for the transcribe voice-memo pipeline.
.\" View with: man transcribe
.TH TRANSCRIBE 1 "2026-07-07" "dotfiles" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
transcribe \- transcribe an iPhone voice memo and file it somewhere
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B transcribe
.RI [ file | name | menu ]
.RI [ destination ]
.RB [ cloud | \-\-cloud ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B transcribe
turns a Voice Memos recording into text and sends it to a destination of your
choosing. Handy for brain dumps, journaling, or capturing ideas on the go.
.PP
By default it grabs the most recent untranscribed recording from the Voice
Memos iCloud sync directory, runs Whisper over it, and appends the result to
today's Obsidian daily note. When it finishes it renames the original audio
with
.RB \(lq (transcribed) \(rq
appended \(em both on disk and in the Voice Memos app \(em so it is skipped
next time and you know it is safe to delete.
.SH ARGUMENTS
Arguments are position-independent; the command figures out which is which.
.TP
.I file
A path to an audio file. If the first non-flag argument is an existing file,
it is transcribed directly (bypasses Voice Memos lookup).
.TP
.I name
The exact title of a recording as shown in the Voice Memos app, e.g.
.RB \(lq "New Recording 80" \(rq .
Looks it up in the Voice Memos database.
.TP
.B menu
Print a numbered list of the 10 most recent untranscribed recordings and prompt
you to pick one.
.PP
With no file or name given, the newest untranscribed recording is used.
.SH DESTINATIONS
.TP
.B daily
Append to today's Obsidian daily note
.RI ( yyyy-mm-dd .md )
under
.IR "~/My Drive/mack/daily" .
This is the default.
.TP
.B notes
Create a new Apple Note titled
.RB \(lq "Brain Dump \- <date>" \(rq
in the
.I Transcriptions
folder.
.TP
.B clipboard
Copy the transcript to the clipboard.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR cloud ", " \-\-cloud
Use the OpenAI Whisper API instead of local Whisper. Requires
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY .
Faster and higher quality; sends audio to OpenAI.
.TP
.BR menu ", " \-\-menu
Show the interactive picker (see
.B menu
above).
.TP
.BR help ", " \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage summary and exit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WHISPER_MODEL
Whisper model size for local mode:
.IR tiny ", " base ", " small ", " medium ", " large .
Defaults to
.IR small .
.TP
.B OPENAI_API_KEY
Required for
.B \-\-cloud
mode.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Local mode needs
.B openai-whisper
.RI ( "pip install openai-whisper" ).
Cloud mode needs
.B curl
and
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY .
Both modes need Voice Memos iCloud sync enabled on your iPhone. Cloud mode also
uses
.B ffmpeg
to convert
.I .qta
recordings to
.IR .m4a .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Transcribe the latest memo to today's daily note (defaults):
.B transcribe
.TP
Use the OpenAI API for a named recording:
.B transcribe \-\-cloud "New Recording 80"
.TP
Pick from a menu and copy to the clipboard:
.B transcribe menu clipboard
.TP
Send a named recording to Apple Notes:
.B transcribe notes "New Recording 80"
.TP
Transcribe an arbitrary audio file:
.B transcribe notes /path/to/audio.m4a
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/Library/Group Containers/group.com.apple.VoiceMemos.shared/Recordings
Voice Memos recordings and the
.I CloudRecordings.db
index.
.TP
.I ~/My Drive/mack/daily/
Obsidian daily notes (the
.B daily
destination).
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on success, non-zero if no recording is found, a dependency is
missing, or transcription fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR whisper (1),
.BR ffmpeg (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Mack McConnell. Source:
.I ~/code/dotfiles/bin/transcribe
